# <destination> <sha256> <url> <archiveType> <stripComponents>
#
# * Set: opentelemetry-sdk 1.34.0 and the closure of its `requires_dist` on
#   PyPI (read 2026-11-20). Every wheel is `py3-none-any`, so one set serves
#   x86_64 and aarch64.
# * Destinations: one `site/<distribution>` directory per wheel. The arms'
#   `python312._pth` names exactly these directories, generated from the same
#   list (`PythonOpenTelemetryWheelDirs`).
# * Layout: a wheel is a zip whose top level is its import packages and its
#   `.dist-info`, which is the layout a directory on `sys.path` needs, so no
#   entry strips a component. Every member path was listed and none is
#   absolute or contains "..".
# * sha256: the digest PyPI publishes for each file, checked 2026-11-20
#   against the downloaded bytes.
